# AGENTS.md (placeholder)

Generic AI agent instructions for the **dev edition** of Ascendo live
in `dev-sync-overlay/ai-instructions/AGENTS.md` and are pushed to a
private Proton overlay via `dev-sync-export.sh`.

Public contributors don't need this file — the public repo is set up
to be productive for any AI assistant (Claude, Codex, Gemini, Cursor,
Aider, Continue.dev, etc.) using only the public docs:
`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `USER_GUIDE.md`, the per-package
`pyproject.toml` files, and the inline docstrings.

If you're a maintainer setting up a fresh dev machine: run
`dev-sync-import.sh` to restore the real `AGENTS.md` alongside the
rest of the dev-edition overlay.

See `CONTRIBUTING.md` for project conventions.
